sharpenedFix:
Two corrections. (1) Gate on the ring, not on the dataset: the tip should be handed back only to a mark that is visibly focused, so a mouse-clicked mark -- focused but not :focus-visible -- clears as it does today. (2) Do not touch hide() at all; hide() is also the blur handler and the pinned gate, and widening it widens the blast radius for no gain. Confine the change to the pointer path, leaving `hide`, `show`, `drop`, `onMove` and the touch pin byte-identical:

    el.addEventListener("pointerleave", (e) => {
      if (e.pointerType === "touch") return;
      const held = document.activeElement;
      if (!pinned && held && held.dataset && held.dataset.tip && held.matches(":focus-visible")) { show(held); return; }
      hide();
    });

This restores the focused mark's name after a pointer crosses it or any sibling, leaves the mouse-only and click-focus paths exactly as they are today, keeps Escape (drop) and touch-away dismissing outright, and because show() resets `showing` to the focused mark it also repairs the finding's secondary measurement -- a later scroll now keeps the label on instead of returning early on !showing.
